        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Well, at the same time it is indeed a `bashd` issue. The value of `vim.NIL` is present if the server explicitly sets `null` to the field (as clarified [here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/34849#issuecomment-3149281532)). This is possible according to the LSP specification in some cases, but this is different from not supplying a field at all. There are no fields in [`CompletionItem`](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#completionItem) that are allowed to be `null` but `bashd` seems to indeed set them like this: [`documentation`](https://github.com/matkrin/bashd/blob/26594c056aa9cf0bde9482f0e2ff06f8580d0cb1/internal/server/completion.go#L80), [`InsertText`](https://github.com/matkrin/bashd/blob/26594c056aa9cf0bde9482f0e2ff06f8580d0cb1/internal/server/completion.go#L186-L187), and [`InsertTextFormat`](https://github.com/matkrin/bashd/blob/26594c056aa9cf0bde9482f0e2ff06f8580d0cb1/internal/server/completion.go#L186-L187). Opening an issue for `bashd` seems like a good idea.\n\nI'll take extra time to see if this is reasonable to be addressed in 'mini.completion'.",
